{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3433","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3433","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3433\",\"parent_revision\":\"b971b24bf8d634e0cd45e41a3c7db091e1c47e4240f9abb420a1fb26e82df6e8\",\"root_revision\":\"b971b24bf8d634e0cd45e41a3c7db091e1c47e4240f9abb420a1fb26e82df6e8\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-06\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe active-task context directory has 27 records, the oldest from 2026-08-22 and the newest from 2026-09-04. Nothing removes them.\\n\\nREPRODUCTION\\n\\n    $ ls ~/.dh/projects/<slug>/context/active-task-*.json | wc -l\\n    27\\n\\nThe hook clears a record when it resolves and completes a task. Records survive whenever that path is not reached: an agent that stopped without the hook resolving it, a registration written under a key the reader never consults, a session that ended abnormally, or a hand-written test id.\\n\\nIMPACT\\n\\nEach stale record is indistinguishable from a live one by name alone, so nothing can decide whether a given file represents work in flight or an abandoned registration from two weeks ago. That blocks any recovery flow that wants to answer \\\"what was in progress when this session died?\\\" and it makes a directory scan increasingly expensive for any resolution strategy that needs one.\\n\\nReaping is only tractable once the record key carries meaning. Under the current session-id key a stale file names nothing actionable; under a plan-and-task key it would name the exact task to reconcile. Depends on the correlation-key defect filed as the P0.\\n\\nUser-provided context: candidate signals for staleness include the started_at field already present in every record, and whether the named task is still in a non-terminal state in its plan.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session audit, 2026-09-06\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"c1906843e7483d067110b074a0439407ca8102d598a51ae0fd40cb6f88966f53\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABTSA-xw\"}"}